WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.389 --> 00:00:04.889
So now you should be able to take the steps that we just went through

2
00:00:04.889 --> 00:00:09.919
and swap out your skeletal meshes to actually see the procedural rigging in action.

3
00:00:09.919 --> 00:00:12.919
And if you build out your rig in a more segmented way,

4
00:00:12.919 --> 00:00:17.920
this is going to allow you to customize the look of each of the controls for each of your body parts

5
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.420
so that you get a more suitable control setup for your characters.

6
00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.820
And just as a recap of the course,

7
00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:28.820
we went over the basic understandings of what procedural rigging means,

8
00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:34.509
and some of the common nodes and functions available to get started with your own procedural rig.

9
00:00:34.509 --> 00:00:36.009
And then we saw this in action,

10
00:00:36.009 --> 00:00:39.509
taking a look at how we might create controls in two slightly different ways

11
00:00:39.509 --> 00:00:45.899
with the spawn control node and the control stack function.

12
00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:49.399
You should now be able to take this information forwards into your own projects

13
00:00:49.399 --> 00:00:52.399
and start building your own procedural rigs.

14
00:00:52.399 --> 00:00:55.899
So thank you for your time, and thank you for attending the course,

15
00:00:55.899 --> 00:00:58.399
and best of luck with your own procedural rigging.
